From db53b4aedc7f7cfdc75d3d70c12c1555f8d5bc66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 31 May 2024 17:58:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 091/135] KVM: TDX: Wait lapic expire when POSTED_INTR_ON set

Call kvm_wait_lapic_expire() when POSTED_INTR_ON is set before TD entry.

Since APIC state is protected for TDX guest, KVM always assumes a timer
IRQ was injected when deciding whether or not to busy wait in
kvm_wait_lapic_expire().  Call kvm_wait_lapic_expire() only when
POSTED_INTR_ON is set to reduce unnecessary wait.

Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
---
v20:
- Split out from patch "KVM: TDX: Implement interrupt injection". (Chao)
---
 arch/x86/kvm/vmx/tdx.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/tdx.c b/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/tdx.c
index c67a6275cc93..4c0f8269e840 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/tdx.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/vmx/tdx.c
@@ -834,9 +834,12 @@ fastpath_t tdx_vcpu_run(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, bool force_immediate_exit)
 
 	trace_kvm_entry(vcpu, force_immediate_exit);
 
-	if (pi_test_on(&tdx->pi_desc))
+	if (pi_test_on(&tdx->pi_desc)) {
 		apic->send_IPI_self(POSTED_INTR_VECTOR);
 
+		kvm_wait_lapic_expire(vcpu);
+	}
+
 	tdx_vcpu_enter_exit(vcpu);
 
 	tdx_user_return_msr_update_cache(vcpu);
