From 2105f08a23f65d5fafb8d87d13e38822071efdb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Jan 2023 19:43:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/135] KVM: selftests: Store initial stack address in struct
 kvm_vcpu

TDX guests' registers cannot be initialized directly using
vcpu_regs_set(), hence the stack pointer needs to be initialized by
the guest itself, running boot code beginning at the reset vector.

We store the stack address as part of struct kvm_vcpu so that it can
be accessible later to be passed to the boot code for rsp
initialization.

